/// Transportable marker trait — see `transport_serialization_design.md` §4.1 and §4.2.
///
/// A program establishes it on one of its inline types with limits, never with code:
///
///     impl Transportable for (:accel, { x: int16, y: int16, z: int16, at_ms: uint64 });
///     impl Transportable for { op: :set | :get, key: string, values: List[int64, mem(normal)] }
///         { max_bytes: 4096, max_depth: 4, max_length: 256 };
///
/// The compiler then derives `encode(F, x)` and `decode(F, frame)` for the type and every wire
/// protocol tag F the program names, such as `(:etf)`. A type with a string or a list in it must
/// give `max_bytes`; `max_length` defaults to it and `max_depth` to 64. Every declaration is a
/// point where foreign bytes become values, so each is reported as an advisory (W2401).

export trait Transportable;
